Portions are adapted from the `examples/buildathon-vta` kit in
verifiable-trust-infrastructure (https://github.com/OpenVTC/verifiable-trust-infrastructure,
Apache-2.0): docker-compose.yml, vta-entrypoint.sh, the scripts in scripts/ and
the client in packages/vta-client. The consumer pipeline in
templates/inbox-verifier follows the usage documented in
dtgwg-trust-tasks-tf (Apache-2.0): GETTING-STARTED.md and trust-tasks-ts/README.md.

Container images. The images this project builds and publishes at ghcr.io/bmiller59
(vta, vtc, mediator; built by .github/workflows/images.yml, or
locally as <name>:local) are built, unmodified, from the upstream sources at the refs pinned in
pins.json, and are distributed under the licences of that software:

- vta and vtc: OpenVTC/verifiable-trust-infrastructure
  (https://github.com/OpenVTC/verifiable-trust-infrastructure, Apache-2.0), at commit
  26d0da81a1ae2df800ee6b9c1806bb3c3c7a9d2f (vta-service-v0.72.0, vtc-service-v0.20.0).
- mediator: affinidi-messaging-mediator
  (https://github.com/affinidi/affinidi-messaging-mediator, Apache-2.0, with its own NOTICE.txt), at
  commit e6e2c63654bb43bb7feb732834702cd940b2bcce (v0.48.0).

The Apache-2.0 text is in LICENSE here and in each upstream repository at those commits; the
upstream NOTICE.txt of the mediator is in its repository at that commit. The images carry the
labels org.opencontainers.image.licenses (Apache-2.0), org.buildathon.upstream-source and
org.opencontainers.image.source, and the exact upstream commit. The images themselves do not
contain copies of the licence files. Both upstream projects enforce a permissive-only licence
allow-list over their Rust dependencies with cargo-deny (deny.toml at the pinned commits: MIT,
Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib and similar); this repository has no deny.toml of its own and has not
audited those transitive crates. Each published image has an SPDX SBOM attestation listing the
packages in it (docs/VERIFY.md). The Debian base layers carry their own package licences.

The TSP client in packages/tsp-client uses @openvtc/pnm-core and @openvtc/vti-tsp-js (Apache-2.0, from
https://github.com/OpenVTC/vta-browser-plugin) as npm dependencies; their sources are not copied here.
